<title>UK: UK managers fear damage if outside EMU - survey.</title>
<headline>UK managers fear damage if outside EMU - survey.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>More than half of Britain's managers -- 53 percent -- fear staying out of a single European currency could be more damaging than joining it, according to a survey by the Institute of Management (IoM).</p>
<p>Forty-nine percent of the 405 managers it polled said they were unsure about the financial implications of a single currency for their company and 58 percent said their organisations had not yet started planning for it.</p>
<p>&quot;Britain's managers are frustrated at the lack of informed debate on the subject,&quot; the IoM said. &quot;Managers believe the government has failed to understand and address these issues.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Richard Murphy, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
